cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use scroot in your research, please cite both the software and the paper below."
title: "scroot: Deterministic, Judge-Free Response Quality Scoring"
abstract: >-
  scroot is an open-source evaluation framework that scores LLM responses
  using factuality classifiers and embedding similarity, producing five
  interpretable quality dimensions (groundedness, completeness, relevance,
  consistency, confidence) and a composite Information Quality Score (IQS),
  without any generative judge model. The score is deterministic, runs fully
  offline on CPU, and incurs zero marginal cost per evaluation.
